cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software in academic work, please cite it using the metadata below."
type: software
title: "DeepTriage-CN: Integrating Clinical Text with Vital Signs for Emergency Department Admission Prediction in an Aging Population"
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2025-05-08"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/DoctorLin1990/DeepTriage-CN"
url: "https://github.com/DoctorLin1990/DeepTriage-CN"
abstract: >
  DeepTriage-CN is a multimodal late-fusion framework that combines frozen
  BERT-Chinese embeddings of nurse-recorded chief complaints with eight
  standardised vital signs to predict hospital admission from the emergency
  department. The model is evaluated on a temporally held-out cohort of
  2 000 encounters with particular attention to the geriatric subgroup
  (age ≥ 65 years).
keywords:
  - emergency department
  - triage
  - hospital admission prediction
  - multimodal learning
  - BERT
  - XGBoost
  - natural language processing
  - clinical decision support
  - aging population
